  () => agent(
    `Map the ACTUAL capabilities of Entire's semantic code-intelligence layer ("entire-sem" provider + the entire-brain consumer). Repo: ${REPO}. Read: docs/semantic_brain_plan.md, docs/semantic_agent_guide.md, docs/semantic_mcp_guide.md, docs/entire_cli_semantic_provider_prompt.md, and the code internal/cli/semantic.go (large — grep for relation types, node kinds, languages, embeddings, clustering, cypher, search) and internal/cli/mcp.go (the MCP tool list) and internal/cli/agent_surface.go.
For EACH area, report has=yes/partial/no/unknown with concrete evidence (file:line or doc quote): parsing engine (tree-sitter? via provider?), graph/node model, RELATION/edge types (calls/imports/extends/implements/route/tool/workflow boundaries — list them), LANGUAGES supported, search (keyword? BM25? EMBEDDINGS? hybrid?), CLUSTERING/community detection, PROCESS/EXECUTION-FLOW tracing from entry points, QUERY interface (cypher? natural language? JSON?), confidence scores on edges, change-impact analysis, multi-repo/workspace, freshness/incremental indexing, refactor/RENAME tooling, privacy/egress stance, MCP tool surface (list the brain_* tools). Be precise about what is ABSENT (e.g. no embeddings, no clustering, no cypher) — that's the point of the comparison.`,
    { label: 'map:entire-sem', phase: 'Map', schema: CAP_SCHEMA }
  ),
  () => agent(
    `Map the ACTUAL capabilities of GitNexus (https://github.com/abhigyanpatwari/GitNexus) — a client-side code-knowledge-graph engine. WebFetch the repo README and any linked docs/architecture pages you can reach (try https://github.com/abhigyanpatwari/GitNexus/blob/main/README.md, /tree/main/docs, and WebSearch "GitNexus code knowledge graph abhigyanpatwari" for blog/details). Confirm and detail each area with evidence (URL or quote): parsing (tree-sitter native + WASM), graph node types (functions/classes/files/folders/COMMUNITIES/PROCESSES), RELATION/edge types (CALLS/IMPORTS/EXTENDS/IMPLEMENTS/MEMBER_OF, confidence 0-1, receiver/self-this resolution), LANGUAGES (the 14 + feature matrix: constructor inference, framework detection, entry-point scoring), SEARCH (BM25 + semantic EMBEDDINGS via transformers.js + RRF — local), CLUSTERING (Leiden communities + cohesion), PROCESS/EXECUTION-FLOW tracing (entry-point → call-chain), QUERY interface (Cypher direct + MCP tools), the MCP TOOL surface (query/context/impact/detect_changes/rename/cypher + group/multi-repo tools — ~16), refactor/RENAME (multi-file coordinated), multi-repo/repo-groups + contract extraction, incremental indexing/repair-fts, privacy/egress (local-only? optional LLM for wiki), wiki generation, deployment (CLI/web/docker/k8s/enterprise). For each, has=yes/partial/no/unknown. Focus on capabilities a CLI/agent user gets — Thomas said to set the web UI aside.`,
    { label: 'map:gitnexus', phase: 'Map', schema: CAP_SCHEMA }
  ),
])

phase('Synthesize')
const fmt = (c) => !c ? '(no data)' : `SYSTEM: ${c.system}\n` + (c.capabilities || []).map((x) => `- [${x.area}] ${x.has}: ${x.detail}`).join('\n') + (c.notes ? `\nNOTES: ${c.notes}` : '')

const synthesis = await agent(
  `You are advising SuhaanT on a reply to Thomas (CEO of Entire), who asked: "GitNexus looks similar to entire-sem — aside from the web UI, what does it offer that we don't, and is that useful?"
Below are capability maps of BOTH systems. Produce:
1. A tight "what GitNexus has that entire-sem does NOT" list — ONLY genuine gaps (skip web UI, docker/k8s/enterprise SaaS as Thomas said set UI aside; focus on engine/agent capabilities).
2. For each gap: is it USEFUL for Entire specifically, given Entire's positioning (local-only/no-egress, brain = durable memory + session history + semantic facts, MCP-first, the provider-boundary design where entire-sem is swappable)? Rate High/Medium/Low usefulness with one-line why.
3. What entire-sem/entire-brain has that GitNexus does NOT (Entire's edge — e.g. session-history/provenance/durable facts, checkpoint-signed sources, no-egress guarantee) — so the reply isn't one-sided.
4. A 2-3 sentence honest bottom line + the top 2-3 things actually worth borrowing.
Be concrete and skeptical; don't recommend adopting something just because it exists. ENTIRE-SEM:\n\n${fmt(entireSem)}\n\nGITNEXUS:\n\n${fmt(gitNexus)}`,
  { label: 'synthesis', phase: 'Synthesize' }
)

return { synthesis, entireSem, gitNexus }

