- Entity extraction (tables, functions, triggers, indexes, policies from migrations): are the tree-sitter node-type queries correct and robust to SQL variations (CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS, schemas like public.foo, quoted identifiers, CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION, dollar-quoted bodies)? Any nil-node / index panics on malformed SQL? Are symbol names/kinds/locations extracted correctly?
